{"id": "q0031", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 4149532189, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "c1188d4ab398808355719c420f025bd920b27aba798f5596eb328457a751cc63", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 2, "query": "Mitchell is making nachos for his family. He buys two bags of chips with 55 chips each. If his family has five members, how many chips does each person get if they all get the same number?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0031.wav", "input_sha256": "7ced3e4c08b561a09d94d3d025af01b41513f1c4d3725350717939273cec2e0f", "input_samples": 238800, "input_s": 14.925, "n_real_chunks": 15, "score": 0.1095, "act": 0.9972, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Okay, so two bags of chip s with 5 5 chips each means he has a total of 2 times 55, which is 11 0 chips. If his family has five members and they all get the same number of chips, we divide the total number of chips by the number of people. So that's 110 divided by 5. That gives us 22. So each person gets 2 2 chips.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 15, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 25, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0031_aggressive_local.wav", "sha256": "ec64e4478c528bde5808f10b065cd7acc5e90b6389776009295adce5246be4b4", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 25.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.069, 1.126, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.07, 2.125, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.069, 3.127, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.073, 4.134, 1, 0, 0