{"id": "q0067", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1665173357, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "c1188d4ab398808355719c420f025bd920b27aba798f5596eb328457a751cc63", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 2, "query": "James likes to check the coin return of the vending machine for change. One day he finds a quarter, two nickels, and 7 dimes. How much money in cents does James have?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0067.wav", "input_sha256": "21a8f15b9712d79881367142340f215c527203a49062e0eafa76a4efb920b66e", "input_samples": 220400, "input_s": 13.775, "n_real_chunks": 14, "score": 0.1641, "act": 0.9984, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So James has a quarter, which is 25 cents. He also has two ni cles, and each nickel is five cents, so that would be 10 cents for the two nickels. And he has seven di mes, and each di me is ten cents, so that would be 70 cents for the seven di mes. If we add all of those together, 25 plus 10 plus 7 0 equals 1 05 cents. So James has 1 05 cents in total.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 13, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 22, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0067_aggressive_local.wav", "sha256": "1ff9f41d140fccb6df70da3d16df41a04c30f3244df82b6d2879015361f6b81d", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 22.04}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.062, 1.113, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.063, 2.117, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.064, 3.114, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.063