{"id": "q0076", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 224167610, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "c1188d4ab398808355719c420f025bd920b27aba798f5596eb328457a751cc63", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 2, "query": "Ryan’s allowance is $6 each week he completes his chores. He did his chores for 3 weeks. Then he bought ice cream cones for himself and 3 friends at $1.25 each. Now they all want to go to the movies and tickets cost $6.50 each. How many movie tickets can Ryan buy?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0076.wav", "input_sha256": "85265e889ec09eee95303cd65f7dc40cedeeaaef80067a53e8c9fcb50d52f509", "input_samples": 344600, "input_s": 21.538, "n_real_chunks": 22, "score": 0.2779, "act": 0.9995, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So Ryan's allowance is six dollars each week he completes his chores. He did his chores for three weeks, so that' s three times six, which equals eighteen dollars. Then he bought ice cream cones for himself and three friends at one dollar twenty five each. That' s four people total, right? So four times one dollar twenty five. Let's see, that' s five dollars. So he spent five dollars on ice cream. Now, after buying the ice cream, how much money does he have left? Eighteen minus five is thirteen dollars remaining. Now, movie tickets cost six dollars fifty each. So we need to figure out how many ticket s he can buy with thirteen dollars. Six dollars fifty is more than half of thirteen, but less than two full tickets. One ticket would be six dollars fifty, leaving him with six dollars fifty remaining, which isn't enough for another ticket. So he can only buy one movie ticket.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 21, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 42, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0076_aggressive_local.wav", "sha256": "05fa757fbc78f9d106dd4c72651c20b67830bec7a7ee75193d806f21f5651b95", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 42.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.062, 1.113, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.065, 2.118, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.065, 3.115, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.065, 4.122, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.063, 5.115, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.063, 6.115, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.071, 7.123, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.078, 8.142, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.065, 9.116, 1, 0, 0], [9, 1, 10.0, 10.066, 10.119, 1, 0, 0], [10, 1, 11.0, 11.065, 11.118, 1, 0, 0], [11, 1, 12.0, 12.068, 12.124, 1, 0, 0], [12, 1, 13.0, 13.067, 13.12, 1, 0, 0], [13, 1, 14.0, 14.069, 14.123, 1, 0, 0], [14, 1, 15.0, 15.066, 15.118, 1, 0, 0], [15, 1, 16.0, 16.068, 16.125, 1, 0, 0], [16, 1, 17.0, 17.067, 17.119, 1, 0, 0], [17, 1, 18.0, 18.069, 18.121, 1, 0, 0], [18, 1, 19.0, 19.068, 19.121, 1, 0, 0], [19, 1, 20.0, 20.068, 20.124, 1, 0, 0], [20, 1, 21.0, 21.068, 21.12, 1, 0, 0], [21, 1, 21.538, 21.605, 22.256, 0, 24000, 0], [22, 0, 22.538, 22.604, 23.206, 0, 24000, 0], [23, 0, 23.538, 23.612, 24.232, 0, 24000, 0], [24, 0, 24.538, 24.606, 25.268, 0, 24000, 0], [25, 0, 25.538, 25.606, 26.245, 0, 24000, 0], [26, 0, 26.538, 26.606, 27.236, 0, 24000, 0], [27, 0, 27.538, 27.605, 28.246, 0, 24000, 0], [28, 0, 28.538, 28.607, 29.133, 0, 24000, 0], [29, 0, 29.538, 29.605, 30.219, 0, 24000, 0], [30, 0, 30.538, 30.608, 31.194, 0, 24000, 0], [31, 0, 31.538, 31.605, 32.236, 0, 24000, 0], [32, 0, 32.538, 32.604, 33.177, 0, 24000, 0], [33, 0, 33.538, 33.606, 34.236, 0, 24000, 0], [34, 0, 34.538, 34.605, 35.155, 0, 24000, 0], [35, 0, 35.538, 35.605, 36.239, 0, 24000, 0], [36, 