{"id": "q0114", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3033147943, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "c1188d4ab398808355719c420f025bd920b27aba798f5596eb328457a751cc63", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 2, "query": "When converting $\\frac{31}{11111}$ to a decimal, the decimal turns out to be a repeating decimal. How many digits repeat in this repeating decimal?\n\nFor example, if you get the repeating decimal $0.\\overline{123},$ then your answer should be $3,$ and if you get $0.436\\overline{7},$ your answer should be $1.$\n\nSolve and give the final answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0114.wav", "input_sha256": "1aac0c2181a56089a0f15195816626de48285ef19be54fcca2f7a7a976ccc4e8", "input_samples": 384600, "input_s": 24.038, "n_real_chunks": 25, "score": 0.9063, "act": 0.9969, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "The repeating decimal for \\(\\frac{31}{1111}\\) has a repeat length equal to the order of \\(10\\) modulo \\(1111\\). Factor: \\[ 1111 = 11 \\cdot 101 \\] , Mod \\(11\\): \\(10^2 \\equiv 1\\), so the period is \\(2\\). , Mod \\(101\\): \\(10^2 = 100 \\equiv -1 \\pmod{101}\\), so \\(10^4 \\equiv 1\\), giving period \\(4\\). Thus the overall repeating period is: \\[ \\text{lcm}(2,4)=4 \\] \\[ \\frac{31}{1111}=0.\\overline{0279} \\] Final answer: \\(\\boxed{4}\\)", "expert_answer": "The repeating decimal for \\(\\frac{31}{1111}\\) has a repeat length equal to the order of \\(10\\) modulo \\(1111\\).\n\nFactor:\n\n\\[\n1111 = 11 \\cdot 101\n\\]\n\n- Mod \\(11\\): \\(10^2 \\equiv 1\\), so the period is \\(2\\).\n- Mod \\(101\\): \\(10^2 = 100 \\equiv -1 \\pmod{101}\\), so \\(10^4 \\equiv 1\\), giving period \\(4\\).\n\nThus the overall repeating period is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{lcm}(2,4)=4\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\frac{31}{1111}=0.\\overline{0279}\n\\]\n\n**Final answer: \\(\\boxed{4}\\)**", "transcript": "When converting frac 31 1111 dollars to a decimal, the decimal turns out to be a repeating decimal. How many digits repeat in this repeating decimal? For example, if you get the repeating decimal 0 overline 123, then your answer should be 3, and if you get 0.436 with overline 7, your answer should b", "asr_s": 4.12, "expert_s": 5.31, "expert_input_samples": 384600, "expert_input_s": 24.038, "expert_input_sha256": "1aac0c2181a56089a0f15195816626de48285ef19be54fcca2f7a7a976ccc4e8", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 4.19, "relay_synth_ms": 76048, "onset_chunk": 24, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 2, "feed_lag_max_ms": 3478, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 6924, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0114_aggressive_relay.wav", "sha256": "ebc32cc29575475d1e9b6d7b0bacb7520fa80ac60a33ca10943db4ea2e3de4ce", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 137.2}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0114_aggressive_candidate.wav", "sha256": "694428ee3d0e665c9006b3c5428102a5b1ac0376344b1fd60a0c50d8ee1e847d", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0114_aggressive_stall.wav", "sha256": "71c703ba99d7b94d2cd268071706fe4a52b88809d5542ffa03dc54df079fad98", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 3.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.067, 1.119, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.062, 2.113, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.065, 3.116, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.065, 4.119, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.068, 5.122, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.065, 6.12, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.065, 7.117, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.066, 8.118, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.073, 9.131, 1, 0, 0], [9, 1, 10.0, 10.068, 10.121, 1, 0, 0], [10, 1, 11.0, 11.078, 11.14, 1, 0, 0], [11, 1, 12.0, 12.08, 12.144, 1, 0, 0], [12, 1, 13.0, 13.075, 13.131, 1, 0, 0], [13, 1, 14.0, 14.082, 14.143, 1, 0, 0], [14, 1, 15.0, 15.079, 15.137, 1, 0, 0], [15, 1, 16.0, 16.076, 16.135, 1, 0, 0], [16, 1, 17.0, 17.077, 17.133, 1, 0, 0], [17, 1, 18.0, 18.081, 18.143, 1, 0, 0], [18, 1, 19.0, 19.081, 19.145, 1, 0, 0], [19, 1, 20.0, 20.08, 20.142, 1, 0, 0], [20, 1, 21.0, 21.08, 21.142, 1, 0, 0], [21, 1, 22.0, 22.072, 22.128, 1, 0, 0], [22, 1, 23.0, 23.076, 23.136, 1, 0, 0], [23, 1, 24.0, 24.082, 24.145, 1, 0, 0], [24, 1, 24.038, 24.221, 24.958, 0, 24000, 0], [25, 0, 25.038, 28.593, 29.377, 0, 24000, 0], [26, 0, 26.038, 29.457, 30.196, 0, 30720, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 24.038, "last_real_feed_done": 24.221, "onset": 24.958, "gate_read_done": 24.958, "fire": 24.958, "candidate_first_pcm": 24.958, "stall_note": 24.961, "stall_first_pcm": 28.516, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 30.196, "expert_req": 24.961, "expert_resp": 34.386, "relay_synth_start": 34.388, "relay_first_pcm": 35.211, "relay_synth_end": 110.436, "first_any_pcm": 24.958, "first_answer_pcm": 35.211, "session_end": 111.136}, "ttfa_answer_s": 11.173, "ttfa_any_s": 0.921}
{"id": "q0144", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3384663650, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "c1188d4ab398808355719c420f025bd920b27aba798f5596eb328457a751cc63", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 2, "query": "Suppose the polynomial\n$$f(x) = a_nx^n + a_{n-1}x^{n-1} + \\cdots + a_2x^2 + a_1x + a_0$$has integer coefficients, and its roots are distinct integers.\n\nGiven that $a_n=2$ and $a_0=66$, what is the least possible value of $|a_{n-1}|$?\n\nSolve and give the final answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0144.wav", "input_sha256": "e888e57e51e9a25af9496b85657e51995827d2223b1d1c8c837f5e6ae9c64986", "input_samples": 289000, "input_s": 18.062, "n_real_chunks": 19, "score": 0.9255, "act": 0.9983, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "The least possible value is \\(-68\\). Since the roots are distinct integers and \\(an=2\\), the polynomial is \\[ 2(x-r1)(x-r2)\\cdots(x-rn) \\] The constant term is \\[ 2(-1)^n r1r2\\cdots rn = 66 \\] so \\[ r1r2\\cdots rn = 33(-1)^n. \\] Also, \\[ a{n-1} = -2(r1+r2+\\cdots+rn). \\] To make \\(a{n-1}\\) as small as possible, we need the sum of the roots as large as possible. Then \\[ 2(x-33)(x-1)=2x^2-68x+66. \\] Thus, \\[ a{n-1}=-68. \\] \\[ \\boxed{-68} \\]", "expert_answer": "The least possible value is **\\(-68\\)**.\n\nSince the roots are distinct integers and \\(a_n=2\\), the polynomial is\n\n\\[\n2(x-r_1)(x-r_2)\\cdots(x-r_n)\n\\]\n\nThe constant term is\n\n\\[\n2(-1)^n r_1r_2\\cdots r_n = 66\n\\]\n\nso\n\n\\[\nr_1r_2\\cdots r_n = 33(-1)^n.\n\\]\n\nAlso,\n\n\\[\na_{n-1} = -2(r_1+r_2+\\cdots+r_n).\n\\]\n\nTo make \\(a_{n-1}\\) as small as possible, we need the sum of the roots as large as possible. The best choice is roots\n\n\\[\n33 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 1,\n\\]\n\nwhich are distinct integers and have product \\(33\\). Then\n\n\\[\n2(x-33)(x-1)=2x^2-68x+66.\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\na_{n-1}=-68.\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-68}\n\\]", "transcript": "Suppose the polynomial of x, a n x to the n plus a n minus 1 x to the n minus 1 plus c dots plus a 2 x squared plus a 1 x plus a 0, has integer coefficients and its roots are distinct integers. Given that a n equals 2 and a 0 equals 66, what is the least possible value of a n minus 1 dollars? Solve ", "asr_s": 1.28, "expert_s": 14.72, "expert_input_samples": 289000, "expert_input_s": 18.062, "expert_input_sha256": "e888e57e51e9a25af9496b85657e51995827d2223b1d1c8c837f5e6ae9c64986", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 14.693, "relay_synth_ms": 50429, "onset_chunk": 18, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 688, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 769, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0144_aggressive_relay.wav", "sha256": "67f639a7cdee145fb18abe22ad5ec708ce95481962abd9a2e091f46158c69962", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 95.28}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0144_aggressive_candidate.wav", "sha256": "46b0d10ceb2015690b21309f493b0218a27418859a529e1187bcdf3db7b5567c", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0144_aggressive_stall.wav", "sha256": "32e36542584410fac41a9ec3f3099a46fbc79c1d9a56219226bbbd0a7631c1c1", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.44}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.079, 1.143, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.088, 2.16, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.082, 3.147, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.081, 4.153, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.088, 5.157, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.083, 6.15, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.083, 7.15, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.079, 8.141, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.078, 9.142, 1, 0, 0], [9, 1, 10.0, 10.083, 10.151, 1, 0, 0], [10, 1, 11.0, 11.086, 11.159, 1, 0, 0], [11, 1, 12.0, 12.08, 12.142, 1, 0, 0], [12, 1, 13.0, 13.076, 13.135, 1, 0, 0], [13, 1, 14.0, 14.074, 14.133, 1, 0, 0], [14, 1, 15.