{"id": "q0233", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 450782047, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "c1188d4ab398808355719c420f025bd920b27aba798f5596eb328457a751cc63", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 2, "query": "Anscombe criticizes Butler on the grounds that:\n\nA. the notion of \"freedom\" is overly simplistic.\nB. the concept of “pleasure” is unclear.\nC. the notion of “legislating for oneself” is absurd.\nD. the idea of \"moral truth\" is a contradiction.\nE. we can't really distinguish between good and evil.\nF. our consciences are fallible.\nG. we really can derive an “ought” from an “is.”\nH. the idea of moral obligations is incoherent.\nI. the concept of \"identity\" is too subjective.\nJ. the concept of \"self\" is ill-defined.\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0233.wav", "input_sha256": "238363efd499e7abbaf7e20182cfddaeb825c73bd2cb38bd79fe49c5213b7455", "input_samples": 544600, "input_s": 34.038, "n_real_chunks": 35, "score": 0.6237, "act": 0.9995, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "F, our consciences are fallible.", "expert_answer": "**F, our consciences are fallible.**", "transcript": "Anscombe criticizes Butler on the grounds that A, the notion of freedom is overly simplistic, B, the concept of pleasure is unclear, C, the notion of legislating for oneself is absurd, D, the idea of moral truth is a contradiction, E, we can't really distinguish between good and evil, F, our conscie", "asr_s": 1.48, "expert_s": 1.92, "expert_input_samples": 544600, "expert_input_s": 34.038, "expert_input_sha256": "238363efd499e7abbaf7e20182cfddaeb825c73bd2cb38bd79fe49c5213b7455", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 1.886, "relay_synth_ms": 234